diff --git a/demos/ecmp_cost.dem b/demos/ecmp_cost.dem
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dfbea70
--- /dev/null
+++ b/demos/ecmp_cost.dem
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# ecmp_cost.dem — 2026-08-13 capacity-cost routing (the canon amendment): the
+# fat pipe wins, and a TRUE different-tier tie still splits by hash. Two
+# compact diamonds (spans 9 <= narrow max 10, so the narrow legs draw legal):
+#   Diamond A (fat-path preference) — ids 0..3:
+#     id 0 = residential res  at (8, 15)   — the source (top)
+#     id 1 = router_basic m1  at (16, 11)  — mid router (upper)
+#     id 2 = router_basic m2  at (16, 19)  — mid router (lower)
+#     id 3 = content_host host at (24, 15) — the sink (bottom)
+#     res->m1 WIDE (cost 5) + m1->host WIDE (cost 5)  = 10  <- the fat path
+#     res->m2 narrow (20)  + m2->host narrow (20)     = 40
+#     From res toward host the fat path is the UNIQUE next hop (no ECMP when
+#     costs differ): every res->host packet rides the WIDE legs; the narrow
+#     legs never carry traffic (the capture's negative pin).
+#   Diamond B (true different-tier tie) — ids 4..7:
+#     id 4 = residential res2 at (32, 15)  — the source
+#     id 5 = router_basic r1  at (40, 11)  — mid router (upper)
+#     id 6 = router_basic r2  at (40, 19)  — mid router (lower)
+#     id 7 = content_host host2 at (48, 15) — the sink
+#     res2->r1 standard(10) + r1->host2 WIDE(5) = 15
+#     res2->r2 WIDE(5)      + r2->host2 standard(10) = 15
+#     EQUAL end-to-end cost across DIFFERENT tiers -> ECMP set of 2: the pure
+#     hash splitmix64(src,dst,class,pkt_id) mod 2 splits the flow across both
+#     paths (flow affinity: same packet -> same path every replay).
+#
+# Transit: packet_bandwidth 30 -> wide (cap 40) = 1 tick/edge, standard (15)
+# = 2 ticks/edge, narrow (5) = 6 ticks/edge. Spawns at 1000/1050/1100/1150ms
+# (ticks 20/21/22/23). The captures pin:
+#   at 1150ms (t23): diamond A has packets mid-flight on the WIDE legs (and
+#     NONE on the narrow legs — the fat-path preference, negative pin);
+#     diamond B has one packet mid-edge on r1->host2 (wide leg) and another
+#     mid-edge on r2->host2 (standard leg) — the tie split, both paths live;
+#   at 1450ms (t29): settled delivery on both diamonds.
+seed 42
+run 2000ms
+fixture off
+spawn_node residential 8 15
+spawn_node router_basic 16 11
+spawn_node router_basic 16 19
+spawn_node content_host 24 15
+spawn_node residential 32 15
+spawn_node router_basic 40 11
+spawn_node router_basic 40 19
+spawn_node content_host 48 15
+at 500ms draw 0 1 wide
+at 500ms draw 0 2 narrow
+at 500ms draw 1 3 wide
+at 500ms draw 2 3 narrow
+at 500ms draw 4 5 standard
+at 500ms draw 4 6 wide
+at 500ms draw 5 7 wide
+at 500ms draw 6 7 standard
+at 1000ms spawn 0 3
+at 1050ms spawn 0 3
+at 1100ms spawn 0 3
+at 1150ms spawn 0 3
+at 1000ms spawn 4 7
+at 1050ms spawn 4 7
+at 1100ms spawn 4 7
+at 1150ms spawn 4 7
+capture at 1150ms
+capture at 1450ms
+expect hash stable
